# The live release colour, imported by the Caddyfile. Spec 011 T7.
#
# This is the ONLY file that changes when a release is promoted or rolled back.
# deploy.sh writes it and runs `caddy reload`, which is graceful: in-flight
# requests finish against the old colour and new ones land on the new one, so
# R10's "served by the previous version throughout" holds with no gap.
#
# Installed at /etc/caddy/upstream.caddy. This .example copy is what the repo
# tracks; the live file is generated, because its whole content is which colour
# is serving right now and that is host state, not source.
#
#   blue  -> 127.0.0.1:5011
#   green -> 127.0.0.1:5012
#
# Caddy sets X-Forwarded-For, X-Forwarded-Proto and X-Forwarded-Host on
# reverse_proxy by default. apps/web only believes them when
# NativeWeb:ForwardedHeaders:KnownProxies names this hop -- unset, every client
# in the world collapses into one rate-limit partition and nothing logs it.
# deploy.sh refuses to promote when that key is missing, for that reason.

reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:5011
